# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from data/forever and tools/lib/professions/gathering. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/skinning
title Skinning 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Ironforge

# Skinning 1-300 for both factions: loops through the densest skinnable beasts
# of the right level for each skill band, with rank training. Skill needed: 1 for
# level 10 and below, (level-10)x10 for 11-20, level x5 above 20.
# Beast lists per zone are curated (tools/lib/professions/gathering/skinning.js);
# levels and spawns come from npcs.json.
#
# Spawns come from the reference data: the Era baseline (pfQuest) plus the
# node spawns Forever's beta sniffs add (Zephras Isle, the starting-area Poor
# Copper Veins and herbs: the Forever TrinityCore world DB); trainer learn skills
# and prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists; recipes and their skill colours
# from the Forever client tables (`forge data professions`).
# ASSUMED: past level 30 (the beta's cap) Forever's spawns are Classic's; nothing
# confirms them yet. In-game check: refine with Polestar_Recorder sessions.
# Ranks ask no character level: Forever's sniffed trainer lists carry none for
# Herbalism, Mining or Skinning, and level 10 for Journeyman crafting and Fishing.
# INGAME: does a gathering trainer ask a level for Expert or Artisan? (our data:
# none; one web guide: Expert 10, Artisan 25).
# Waypoints are Era-frame (`coords era`); the engine converts them where Forever
# changed a map frame, and a map without an Era frame (Zephras Isle) compiles live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice

step Learn Skinning
  tip Any Skinning trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice Skinning at any level (10c), and so does the Junior Skinning Trainer in each starting area; the arrow picks the nearest. Buy a Skinning Knife from a trade goods or general vendor: keep it in your bags, you cannot skin without it. The first-hour quest of each starting area (Rascally Rodents, Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery, The Woodland Protector, Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise, A Humble Task, Marla's Last Wish) offers Pelt Collecting for Beginners as a reward: reading it gives 2 skill, up to 15. Trade goods vendors and the junior trainers sell the Apprentice's Skinning Satchel, a four-slot bag for leather and hides (25c). If you sat at your starting area's campfire for The Great Outdoors, the camping guide there also offers Camping 101: Skinning: hand it in to the skinning trainer it names once you reach skill 20, for the Camp Chair recipe.
  train Skinning Apprentice
  buy 7005 x1 nearest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Skinning 1-50

